From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: ps5: a no-access page does not make its host page read-only

Patch 1122 maps a 16 KiB host page read-only when any committed 4 KiB page in
it is not writable, so a write tracker sees every first write. A committed
no-access page counted too, though nothing tracks writes with one, and the
host page then faulted on every write to its writable pages. Mono keeps its
hazard pointer table on such a host page: every hazard pointer write faulted
and ran as one stepped instruction, about 9,000 a second, and a .NET game
spent about 40 s starting. A no-access page (committed, without read, write,
write-copy, execute or guard) no longer counts; read-only, write-watched and
guard pages still do, so trackers and stack guards fault as before.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c	2026-10-24 20:35:15.587727514 -0400
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c	2026-10-24 20:35:15.597094896 -0400
@@ -2579,8 +2579,13 @@
         {
             BYTE vprot = (vprot_ptr[i] & ~clear) | set;
             /* set reaches the whole host page (mprotect_range rounds): only pages committed themselves count; a free
-             * page beside a 4 KiB view took wineboot's write to KUSER_SHARED_DATA (usd-diag-2026-10-14-02). */
-            if ((vprot_ptr[i] & VPROT_COMMITTED) && !(get_unix_prot( vprot ) & PROT_WRITE)) break;
+             * page beside a 4 KiB view took wineboot's write to KUSER_SHARED_DATA (usd-diag-2026-10-14-02). A no-access
+             * page (committed, no read, write or execute, no guard) does not count either: nothing tracks writes with it,
+             * and Mono's hazard table, writable pages beside committed no-access ones, faulted on every hazard pointer
+             * write, about 9,000 a second, and a .NET game took 40 s to start (2026-10-24). Read-only,
+             * write-watched and guard pages still count. */
+            if ((vprot_ptr[i] & VPROT_COMMITTED) && !(get_unix_prot( vprot ) & PROT_WRITE) &&
+                (vprot & (VPROT_READ | VPROT_WRITE | VPROT_WRITECOPY | VPROT_EXEC | VPROT_GUARD))) break;
         }
         if (i < host_page_size / page_size && (view = find_view( addr, 0 )) && !(view->protect & SEC_IMAGE))
             prot &= ~PROT_WRITE;
